-- label_set: 1 = importance scale, 2 = appropriateness scale

DO $$
DECLARE
  v_s01 UUID; v_s02 UUID; v_s03 UUID; v_s04 UUID; v_s05 UUID;
  v_s06 UUID; v_s07 UUID; v_s08 UUID; v_s09 UUID; v_s10 UUID;
BEGIN

  -- S01: Pharmaceutical dinner invitation
  VALUES ('After a busy diabetes clinic, foundation year two doctor Sarah Khan is approached by a pharmaceutical sales representative who invites her and three colleagues to an all-expenses-paid ''educational dinner'' at a high-end restaurant the following week. The representative mentions there will be a brief talk about a new diabetes medication, but the main purpose is networking. Sarah''s department recently switched to prescribing this company''s medications.

How appropriate is each of the following responses by Sarah?')
  RETURNING id INTO v_s01;

  -- S02: Patient recording consultation
  VALUES ('Daniyaal, a fourth-year medical student on a GP placement, notices halfway through a consultation that the patient has propped a phone on the desk and is recording the entire conversation. The patient has not mentioned this to the GP, who has not noticed. The GP is currently explaining a serious diagnosis.

How important to take into account are each of the following considerations for Daniyaal when deciding how to respond?')
  RETURNING id INTO v_s02;

  -- S03: Classmate self-medicating with antibiotics
  VALUES ('While tidying up after a study session in the medical school library, third-year student Marcus notices that his classmate Aleena has left a half-used strip of antibiotic tablets in her bag. Earlier that day Aleena mentioned having a ''nasty chest infection'' but said she did not want to miss any teaching to see a GP. Marcus knows Aleena''s older brother is a GP.

How appropriate is each of the following responses by Marcus?')
  RETURNING id INTO v_s03;

  -- S04: Cash gift from grateful patient
  VALUES ('On her last day on the elderly care ward, foundation year two doctor Olamide is approached by Mr Henderson, a patient she has cared for over six weeks. He hands her a sealed envelope and says, with tears in his eyes, that this is ''a small thank-you'' for everything she has done. The envelope is thick and feels as though it contains cash.

How important to take into account are each of the following considerations for Olamide when deciding how to respond?')
  RETURNING id INTO v_s04;

  -- S05: Consultant making jokes about anaesthetised patient
  VALUES ('During a long abdominal surgery that fourth-year medical student Theo is observing, the consultant surgeon makes a series of jokes about the anaesthetised patient''s weight, drawing laughter from two of the theatre nurses. The patient is unconscious and unaware. Theo feels uncomfortable but is aware that the consultant supervises his upcoming clinical assessment.

How appropriate is each of the following responses by Theo?')
  RETURNING id INTO v_s05;

  -- S06: Group member not contributing to dissertation
  VALUES ('Naomi is part of a six-person group preparing a final-year dissertation presentation. With three days to go, one member, Toby, has missed every group meeting in the past fortnight and has not submitted the section he was assigned. Naomi has tried messaging him twice with no reply. The rest of the group is becoming increasingly frustrated.

How appropriate is each of the following responses by Naomi?')
  RETURNING id INTO v_s06;

  -- S07: Conscientious objection to terminations
  VALUES ('Aiyana, a foundation year one doctor, has been rostered to a gynaecology clinic that includes assisting with elective terminations of pregnancy. She has strong personal beliefs that make her uncomfortable with this work and is considering raising a conscientious objection with her supervisor. The clinic is short-staffed and has a long waiting list.

How important to take into account are each of the following considerations for Aiyana when deciding how to respond?')
  RETURNING id INTO v_s07;

  -- S08: Falsified dental logbook
  VALUES ('Reviewing his classmate''s patient logbook before they both submit it for end-of-year sign-off, fourth-year dental student Joon-ho realises that his classmate Faisal has logged three restorations Joon-ho is certain he never performed. Two of the entries have a supervising dentist''s name attached. Faisal previously mentioned he was behind on his clinical numbers.

How appropriate is each of the following responses by Joon-ho?')
  RETURNING id INTO v_s08;

  -- S09: Supervisor requesting outlier data removal
  VALUES ('An intercalated medical student is finalising the analysis for her supervisor''s research paper, which is being submitted to a high-impact journal next week. Her supervisor, who is also chair of her department, has asked her to remove three ''outlier'' data points that he says are clearly errors. She has rerun the analysis without them and can see that the results now reach statistical significance, where they previously did not.

How important to take into account are each of the following considerations for the student when deciding how to respond?')
  RETURNING id INTO v_s09;

  -- S10: Withdrawn flatmate
  VALUES ('For the past three weeks, Idris''s flatmate Ben has been increasingly withdrawn — eating alone in his room, missing classes, and sleeping through the day. Last night, Idris overheard Ben crying. The two are friendly but not especially close, and Ben''s family lives several hundred miles away.

How appropriate is each of the following responses by Idris?')
  RETURNING id INTO v_s10;

END $$;

