  v_s06 UUID; v_s07 UUID; v_s08 UUID; v_s09 UUID; v_s10 UUID;
BEGIN

  -- S01: Faulty ECG machine
  VALUES ('During his shift on a busy ward, Tobi, a foundation year one doctor, notices that one of the ECG machines occasionally produces erratic readings. He has heard nurses joke about it being ''temperamental'' for weeks, but it has not been taken out of service. The ward sister tells him a replacement has been ordered but is awaiting budget approval, so the machine remains in regular use.

How appropriate is each of the following responses by Tobi?')
  RETURNING id INTO v_s01;

  -- S02: Patient stopping metformin for herbal supplement
  VALUES ('A 67-year-old man with type 2 diabetes attends his GP review with Aisha, a fourth-year medical student observing. He explains that he has stopped taking his metformin and is instead using a herbal supplement recommended by a friend. He says he feels ''much better'' and does not want any blood tests today. The GP looks visibly frustrated.

How important to take into account are the following considerations for Aisha when reflecting on the consultation?')
  RETURNING id INTO v_s02;

  -- S03: Student making racist remark about patient
  VALUES ('On a ward placement, two third-year medical students, Hayden and Marcus, are reviewing patient files in a side room. Marcus mutters a racially derogatory remark about an elderly patient he has just seen, then laughs and continues writing his notes. Hayden is shocked and unsure how Marcus would react if challenged.

How appropriate is each of the following responses by Hayden?')
  RETURNING id INTO v_s03;

  -- S04: F1 asked to prescribe chemotherapy beyond competence
  VALUES ('Dr Halima Ndiaye, a foundation year one doctor on a surgical ward, is asked by the on-call consultant to prescribe a chemotherapy drug for a complex patient. The consultant explains that the registrar is in theatre and says, ''Just write it up — it''s straightforward and I''ll countersign later.'' Dr Ndiaye has never prescribed chemotherapy before and feels uneasy.

How appropriate is each of the following responses by Dr Ndiaye?')
  RETURNING id INTO v_s04;

  -- S05: Aggressive family member in corridor
  VALUES ('Dr Lin, a foundation year two doctor, has just informed a family that their elderly mother''s condition has deteriorated overnight. The patient''s adult son becomes loudly verbally aggressive in the corridor, accusing the team of negligence and demanding to see the consultant immediately. Other patients and visitors are looking on uncomfortably.

How important to take into account are the following considerations for Dr Lin in deciding how to respond?')
  RETURNING id INTO v_s05;

  -- S06: Student photographing patient notes
  VALUES ('While on a hospital placement, Tomás, a fifth-year medical student, sees a fellow student briefly photograph the front page of a patient''s paper notes. The other student tells him cheerfully that they''re ''just for revision'' and that he''s anonymised them by photographing only part of the page. Tomás knows the page captured includes the patient''s full name and date of birth.

How appropriate is each of the following responses by Tomás?')
  RETURNING id INTO v_s06;

  -- S07: Bruising on dental patient suggesting domestic abuse
  VALUES ('A patient, Mrs Whitaker, attends a routine dental check-up. During the examination, Aanya, a final-year dental student, notices what appear to be fingertip-shaped bruises on the patient''s neck and lower jaw. Mrs Whitaker laughs nervously and says she ''walked into a door'' when Aanya asks. Her partner, who drove her, is sitting in the waiting area and earlier appeared controlling.

How important to take into account are the following considerations for Aanya in deciding how to respond?')
  RETURNING id INTO v_s07;

  -- S08: F1 colleague consistently late to handover
  VALUES ('Dr Aroha, a foundation year one doctor, has noticed that a fellow F1 doctor, Dr Patel, is regularly 15–20 minutes late to morning handover. The night team has had to wait, and on two occasions Dr Aroha has noticed the night registrar leave key information unsaid because they had to rush to another commitment. Dr Patel has not been challenged by anyone about the lateness.

How appropriate is each of the following responses by Dr Aroha?')
  RETURNING id INTO v_s08;

  -- S09: Consultant potentially in relationship with current patient
  VALUES ('While catching up over coffee, a fellow medical student tells Yusuf that she has seen Dr Crawford, a respected consultant on their current placement, holding hands with one of his current outpatient patients in town. The student asks Yusuf not to tell anyone because she ''doesn''t want to start a rumour''. Yusuf knows the patient is still under Dr Crawford''s care.

How appropriate is each of the following responses by Yusuf?')
  RETURNING id INTO v_s09;

  -- S10: Medical student approached by journalist after shift
  VALUES ('Walking out of the hospital after a shift, Eshe, a fourth-year medical student, is approached by a local journalist who is investigating a recent serious incident on the ward where she has been placed. The journalist asks her, off the record, what staff have been saying about it. Eshe has heard several frank conversations among colleagues about the incident.

How important to take into account are the following considerations for Eshe in deciding how to respond?')
  RETURNING id INTO v_s10;

END $$;

