BEGIN

  -- S01: Patient disclosing domestic abuse to medical student
  VALUES ('During a GP placement, a 32-year-old patient confides to Akin, a fourth-year medical student observing the consultation, that her partner has been hitting her over recent months. She asks Akin not to mention this to the GP because she just wanted someone to talk to and is worried it will make things worse at home. The GP has briefly stepped out of the room to fetch a leaflet.

How appropriate is each of the following responses by Akin?')
  RETURNING id INTO v_s01;

  -- S02: Jehovah's Witness refusing blood transfusion
  VALUES ('A patient scheduled for major elective surgery is a Jehovah''s Witness and has stated clearly that she will not accept a blood transfusion under any circumstances, even if her life is at risk. The consultant believes the surgery should still go ahead, with appropriate planning to minimise blood loss. Hannah, a final-year medical student, is shadowing the team during the pre-operative consultation.

How important to take into account are the following considerations for the medical team in this situation?')
  RETURNING id INTO v_s02;

  -- S03: Colleagues mocking patient in doctors' mess
  VALUES ('While taking a break in the doctors'' mess, Dr Marek, a foundation year one doctor, hears two of his fellow F1 colleagues making jokes about a patient''s appearance and weight, and mimicking the patient''s voice. The patient is currently an inpatient on their ward. Several other staff members are also in the mess at the time.

How appropriate is each of the following responses by Dr Marek?')
  RETURNING id INTO v_s03;

  -- S04: Controlled drugs discrepancy at end of night shift
  VALUES ('At the end of a busy night shift, Dr Lin, a foundation year two doctor, is asked to help check the controlled drugs register before handover. She notices that the recorded stock of morphine ampoules does not match the actual count in the cupboard — there are three fewer than the register indicates. The senior nurse on shift, who has just arrived, suggests it is probably just a paperwork error from the previous shift.

How important to take into account are the following considerations for Dr Lin in this situation?')
  RETURNING id INTO v_s04;

  -- S05: Patient passing personal note to dental student
  VALUES ('After completing a routine dental check-up at a teaching hospital clinic, a young patient discreetly slips a folded piece of paper to Maya, a third-year dental student. Once the patient has left, Maya unfolds the note and finds his phone number along with a message saying he would love to grab a coffee sometime. The patient is around the same age as Maya and has another appointment scheduled in two weeks.

How appropriate is each of the following responses by Maya?')
  RETURNING id INTO v_s05;

  -- S06: Doctor asked to prescribe for family member
  VALUES ('Dr Tomas, a foundation year one doctor, is at a family gathering when his mother takes him aside. She has been having trouble sleeping for several weeks and asks him to write her a private prescription for zopiclone, saying she does not want to bother her own GP and that it must be safe because it is just for sleep. She has not been formally assessed by anyone for her insomnia.

How appropriate is each of the following responses by Dr Tomas?')
  RETURNING id INTO v_s06;

  -- S07: Child used as interpreter in sensitive GP consultation
  VALUES ('During a GP placement, Ravi, a fourth-year medical student, sits in on a consultation with a 34-year-old woman who speaks limited English. She has come in to discuss unspecified women''s pains and has brought her 9-year-old son to translate. The GP, running a packed clinic, appears ready to proceed with the child translating.

How important to take into account are the following considerations for the GP in this situation?')
  RETURNING id INTO v_s07;

  -- S08: Racial discrimination in tutorial group
  VALUES ('During a small group university tutorial, Lerato notices that one of her group members, Ben, repeatedly interrupts and dismisses ideas from another member, Dapo, while accepting similar ideas when raised by white students. After the session, Dapo quietly mentions to Lerato that this has been a recurring pattern across multiple tutorials and he is starting to dread group work.

How appropriate is each of the following responses by Lerato?')
  RETURNING id INTO v_s08;

  -- S09: Flatmate plagiarising dental school essay
  VALUES ('Jonas walks into the kitchen one evening and sees his flatmate, Carlos, hunched over his laptop with multiple browser tabs open. Looking over his shoulder, Jonas realises Carlos is copying entire paragraphs from various websites directly into the essay he is meant to be submitting to his dental school the next morning. Carlos notices Jonas looking, laughs, and says everyone does it and his deadline is too tight.

How important to take into account are the following considerations for Jonas in this situation?')
  RETURNING id INTO v_s09;

  -- S10: Student unwell on morning of placement assessment
  VALUES ('At 6am on the morning of an important placement assessment, Sienna, a third-year medical student, wakes up with severe vomiting and diarrhoea. She has been counting on this assessment as a chance to demonstrate her clinical skills to a strict consultant who only sees students once per term. The placement is on a ward that includes elderly and immunocompromised patients.

How appropriate is each of the following responses by Sienna?')
  RETURNING id INTO v_s10;

END $$;

