  RETURNING id INTO v_s07;

  -- S08: Patient making racist remark about consultant
  VALUES ('During a hospital placement, third-year medical student Conor is observing the surgical clinic when a new patient enters and refuses to be seen by the consultant, Dr Adesanya, demanding instead ''a doctor who''s actually from this country.'' Dr Adesanya remains professional but is visibly affected; the clinic nurse looks uncertain about how to react.

How appropriate is each of the following responses by Conor?')
  RETURNING id INTO v_s08;

  -- S09: Writing reference for unreliable colleague
  VALUES ('Specialty trainee Esi is asked by her colleague Marcus to provide a written reference for a research fellowship he is applying for. Esi has worked alongside Marcus for the past six months and likes him personally, but during that time he has cancelled shifts at short notice on several occasions and arrived late to handovers, leaving others to cover. The application form asks the referee to comment honestly on the applicant''s reliability and teamwork.

How appropriate is each of the following responses by Esi?')
  RETURNING id INTO v_s09;

  -- S10: Classmate asking to share notes in prohibited open-book essay
  VALUES ('In the second year of their joint degree, Yusuf and Lara are both working on an open-book essay assessment whose guidance explicitly forbids sharing notes, summaries, or templates between students under penalty of being treated as collusion. Two days before the deadline, Lara messages Yusuf asking if she can have a ''quick look'' at his notes, just to help her structure her own answer.

How important to take into account are the following considerations for Yusuf when deciding how to respond?')
  RETURNING id INTO v_s10;

